/// The disturbance vectors SHA-1 collision detection checks, generated by `parse_bitrel` from
/// the data of `tools/data/3565` of Marc Stevens's and Dan Shumow's `sha1collisiondetection`:
/// the 16 of type I, `I(43,0)` to `I(52,0)`, then the 16 of type II, `II(45,0)` to `II(56,0)`,
/// each record's [`mask_bit`](DvInfoRef::mask_bit) its index, followed by the record whose
/// type is `0`, which ends the table for `sha1.c`'s C.
///
/// Immutable: C reads it (`sha1_process`) and writes none of it. Once the module has switched
/// from C, it is the one `sha1_dvs` the remaining C reads, through its export.
///
/// Replaces `glb::sha1_dvs`
#[doc(alias = "sha1_dvs")]
#[cfg(not(feature = "ffi-export-src-util-hash-sha1dc-ubc-check-c"))]
pub static SHA1_DVS: [DvInfo; DV_COUNT] = DVS;

#[cfg(feature = "ffi-export-src-util-hash-sha1dc-ubc-check-c")]
pub use self::ffi_export::sha1_dvs as SHA1_DVS;

/// Checks an expanded message block against the unavoidable bitconditions of the disturbance
/// vectors of [`SHA1_DVS`], and returns the mask, one word ([`DVMASKSIZE`]), whose bit of
/// each vector ([`mask_bit`](DvInfoRef::mask_bit), named by the `DV_*_BIT` constants) is set
/// where every one of its conditions holds: those are the vectors `sha1.c` recompresses the
/// block with, to tell a collision attack. Of the block's 80 words, it reads words 35 to 64.
///
/// A statement-for-statement translation of the C, which `parse_bitrel` generated from the
/// conditions' data, in the C's order: each condition clears the bits of the vectors it fails,
/// with the C's wrapping 32-bit arithmetic, and those that the C guards with a test of the
/// mask are skipped where it is clear.
///
/// # Examples
///
/// The vectors `sha1_process` recompresses a block with, read from the table as it reads it:
///
/// ```
/// use libgit2_crustify::libgit2::src::util::hash::sha1dc::ubc_check::{SHA1_DVS, ubc_check};
///
/// // A block whose words are all equal meets the conditions of no vector.
/// let [mask] = ubc_check(&[0; 80]);
/// let selected = SHA1_DVS
